ZeRO-DP has three main optimization stages (as depicted in Figure 1), which correspond to the partitioning of optimizer states, gradients, and parameters. When enabled cumulatively:
1) Optimizer State Partitioning (Po Pos ): 4x memory reduction, same communication volume as DP;
2) Add Gradient Partitioning (Po Pos+g ): 8x memory reduction, same communication volume as DP;
3) Add Parameter Partitioning (Po Pos+g+p ): Memory reduction is linear with DP degree Nd . For example, splitting across 64 GPUs (Nd = 64) will yield a 64x memory reduction. There is a modest 50% increase in communication volume.
